    "fact_rationales": {
      "F15": "Skin biopsy findings are crucial for diagnosing lymphomas with cutaneous involvement, and all candidates are potential considerations.",
      "F16": "Intravascular atypical cells on hematoxylin-eosin stained sections and CD56 immunostaining are highly suggestive of intravascular large B-cell lymphoma.",
      "F6": "New skin eruption is more typical of lymphomas with cutaneous involvement, such as subcutaneous panniculitis-like T-cell lymphoma and primary cutaneous gamma-delta T-cell lymphoma.",
      "F7": "Widespread, nontender, erythematous patches and thin plaques with telangiectases and hyperpigmentation are more typical of lymphomas with cutaneous involvement, such as subcutaneous panniculitis-like T-cell lymphoma and primary cutaneous gamma-delta T-cell lymphoma."
